{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release-critique","packet_sha256":"90def7ab0b7ee10bfcc26951c33b67f6417b5195bcf7d3a8ccaf68fa0ae26c71","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"bf9bcb5c76db92e32d32409cbb3a3d75cf885c18607d1bf93a80bf5a65e82316","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"blocked-marker-tail-eviction-disables-linger-enforcement","severity":"high","summary":"Blocked-linger enforcement is not durable: after the first BLOCKED observation, the watch still requires the marker to remain in the bounded log tail on every later poll. If a lingering executor emits enough output to evict the marker before the grace expires, the lane is never stopped for lingering after BLOCKED.","evidence":["scripts/task_run/task_run_progress.py: LaneProgressWatch.tick sets `_blocker_at` when `progress[\"blocker\"]` is present, but has no cumulative stored blocker value.","scripts/task_run/task_run_progress.py: subsequent ticks enter the blocked-grace branch only when the current bounded `_tail_text` scan still returns a blocker; otherwise execution falls through to the CONTRACT-READ/no-progress logic.","scripts/task_run/task_run_progress.py: `_tail_text` reads only the last 64 KiB, so continued output can remove the BLOCKED marker from observation.","tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_implementation_lane.py tests phase-marker aging but does not test a BLOCKED marker aging out during its grace period."],"action":"Persist the first observed blocker in LaneProgressWatch and enforce the grace deadline from that cumulative state even after the marker leaves the tail. Add a regression test that observes BLOCKED, replaces or grows the log beyond the tail window, advances to the grace deadline, and verifies a stop reason."},{"id":"missing-live-blocked-linger-proof","severity":"medium","summary":"The packet does not provide live end-to-end proof that an actually running lane which declares BLOCKED is killed after the grace period and receipted with both its declared blocker and guard stop outcome.","evidence":["tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_implementation_lane.py: `test_lingering_blocked_lane_is_stopped_after_grace` drives `tick()` directly and never starts a subprocess, invokes the kill callback, or completes a receipt.","The live subprocess test `test_stalled_lane_is_killed_live_and_receipted` covers the no-progress path, not the blocked-linger path.","The packet includes no execution results or other live proof artifact; source and test text alone do not establish that the blocked-linger round trip works."],"action":"Add and run an end-to-end test using a stub executor that emits BLOCKED and sleeps, with a short blocked grace and poll interval; assert early process termination, `progress_guard.stop_reason`, preservation of the declared `lane_progress.blocker`, failed/ineligible completion, and elapsed time below the executor timeout."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Transcript blocker takes precedence over the guard stop reason in `apply_lane_receipt`.","bin":"acceptable-with-existing-evidence","disposition":"The declared blocker remains the primary lane reason while `progress_guard.stop_reason` separately records forced termination. This is not itself a blocker, provided the end-to-end receipt proves both fields survive."},{"concern":"A non-positive no-progress budget might disable blocked-linger enforcement.","bin":"not-a-finding","disposition":"The blocked-linger branch is independent of `budget_seconds`; disabling the no-progress stop does not disable blocked-grace handling."},{"concern":"Blocked grace configuration is not exposed in the guard receipt.","bin":"follow-up","disposition":"The receipt records budget and poll settings but omits `blocked_grace_seconds`. This weakens auditability, though it is secondary to the enforcement escape and missing live proof."}],"next_move":"Block release until BLOCKED observation is cumulative across bounded-tail eviction and a real subprocess round trip proves lingering-block termination and terminal receipt behavior.","non_claims":["No workspace files were read or modified; this judgment uses only the identity-bound inline payload.","No test suite or live task-run command was executed.","This review does not assess behavior outside the six bound semantic input paths.","Goal evidence is not goal-bound, as stated by the supplied lineage."]}
